nt data.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2033\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies my administrative-throughput cap of 400-700k/yr and my entries-to-wage elasticity of ~0.1. The care constraint then clears substantially on migration rather than on wages or rationing, so: CQ1's wage conjunct falls from 0.25 to ~0.12 (migrant entry dilutes the F+Q median hard) and CQ1 drops from 16 to ~9; CQ2's OECD leg falls ~5pp and CQ2 to ~32; CQ3 P50 up ~+0.15pp; and hypothesis plank (b) rises from 13 toward ~25 on the remittance leg while falling further on the 'blocks' wording.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"Philippine IT-BPM headcount and revenue (IBPAP annual roadmap data) and Indian IT-BPM export revenue (NASSCOM): does Philippine BPO headcount fall below 1.3M while sector revenue falls more than 15% below its 2026 level in nominal USD, AND do Philippine remittances fail to exceed $45bn/yr?\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2033\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Confirms the virtual leg's downside while falsifying my physical-leg offset, which is the specific netting my score of 13 on plank (b) rests on. Plank (b) would move from 13 to ~45 (the 'severely' word becomes defensible even though 'blocks' stays wrong). It would also mean the OECD care gap is NOT being filled by migration, so CQ1's wage conjunct rises from 0.25 to ~0.34 and CQ1 from 16 to ~21, CQ2's OECD leg rises ~4pp, and CQ6-C rises from 23 to ~28 at B's expense.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"Divergence check on the actual CQ1 wage measure: OECD/national real median hourly earnings by ISIC sector. Does the cumulative 2025-to-year-end real median hourly gap between (F+Q) and (J+K+M) exceed +5.0pp, and is the DECOMPOSITION published showing whether within-job wage growth or composition dominates?\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2032\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"A gap above +5.0pp by 2032 implies my composition wedge of -7 to -9pp is overstated and the path to +10pp by 2036 is open: CQ1's wage conjunct rises from 0.25 to ~0.45 and CQ1 from 16 to ~27. A gap below +2.